THE GOAL HERE IS TO CREATE A SIMPLE WASM-LIKE MACHINE IN ORDER TO
LEARN MORE COMPLETELY WHAT WASM DOES AND HOW.

Rewriting in Rust, compiled to WebAssembly for the browser. Phased,
educational iterations:

- Phase 1 ✅ i32 stack machine: Push, Pop, Drop, Add, Sub, Mul, Div
    - ✅ crates/wasmvm-core scaffolded with wasm-bindgen
    - ✅ wasm-pack build wired to static/src/wasmvm-pkg
    - ✅ frontend loads native wasm module (no Pyodide)
- Phase 2: more instructions and all four types (i32, i64, f32, f64)
    - comparisons (Eq, Eqz, Lt, Le, Gt, Ge), bitwise (AND, OR, XOR)
    - per-instruction type selection in the UI
- Phase 3: linear memory
    - pages, Grow, load/store at offset
    - visual representation of memory in the UI

Legacy Python notes from the previous iteration are preserved below.

